@@ -6,3 +6,16 @@ package holds the order book, in TypeScript; the shop's website and its staff to
 `src/index.ts`.
 
 Prices are integer cents everywhere. Run the tests with `npm test`.
+
+## Discount codes
+
+An order takes one discount code at most: `orders.applyCode(orderNumber, code)` gives the order the code, and a
+second code replaces the first. The order's totals show the discount as `discountCents` (0 without a code) and
+`totalCents` as items minus discount plus shipping.
+
+- `SPRING10` takes 10 % off the items, rounded to the nearest cent with a half cent rounding up.
+- `WELCOME5` takes 5.00 € off the items, only on an order whose items come to 30.00 € or more.
+
+An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused with an error that says why, and the order keeps
+what it had. Codes match ignoring case and surrounding spaces. The discount never touches shipping: whether an
+order ships free is decided on its items before any discount.
